+
+### Address-scoped result idempotency (0.4, oa-06)
+
+A result's first-write-wins identity is `(storage namespace, complete MailboxKey,
+caller idempotency key)`. Tenant, user and session all participate; `None` and
+an empty optional identifier are distinct. Two addresses may reuse the same
+caller key independently. Within one address, retries retain the first result
+even after consume/reopen, until its original TTL elapses; a no-TTL fence stays
+permanent. Expiry at one address never releases another address's fence.
+`DeliveryOutcome` remains `Stored` or `Duplicate`; unkeyed delivery is unchanged.
+
+The pure-core mapping type is
+`prometheus_parking_lot_core::LegacyIdempotencyOwner` (`new(caller_key, key)`,
+public `idempotency_key: String` and `key: MailboxKey`, serde with unknown fields
+rejected). It is exported by the core crate, not by the facade's `core::backend`.
+The supported backend entry points are:
+
+| Entry | Upgrade behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PgResultMailbox::<T>::migrate(&pool).await` | Fresh protocol-2 schema or locked conversion using only uniquely proven retained-result owners; refuses unresolved active legacy fences. |
+| `PgResultMailbox::<T>::migrate_with_idempotency_owners(&pool, &owners).await` | Explicit evidence is `&[(String, LegacyIdempotencyOwner)]`; each outer string is the exact PG mailbox name. |
+| `EmbeddedStore::open(path)` / `open_with_clock(path, clock)` | Create/reopen schema 2; refuse schema 1 rather than converting it silently. |
+| `EmbeddedStore::open_with_idempotency_owners(path, &owners)` / `open_with_clock_and_idempotency_owners(path, clock, &owners)` | Explicit schema-1 conversion with `&[LegacyIdempotencyOwner]`, or schema-2 mapping validation. |
+
+Legacy consumed tombstones contain no owner address. Unexpired tombstones
+require authoritative ownership evidence or migration refuses atomically;
+permanent consumed tombstones cannot be resolved merely by waiting. A retained
+row proves an owner only when its caller key and original expiry generation
+match exactly. Multiple candidates require a mapping selecting one candidate.
+Existing results, original expiry, consumed fences, queue identity and ordering
+are preserved. Expired ownerless fences remain legacy provenance rather than
+being assigned an invented tenant.
+
+Resolved-owner provenance remains independent of active fences: replaying a
+recorded mapping validates it without resetting TTL or resurrecting an evicted
+fence. Stop old readers/writers before conversion. Old PG mutation SQL is
+rejected at the database boundary; the old redb open protocol rejects schema 2.
+Rollback requires the untouched pre-upgrade backup with new writers stopped;
+it does not recover subsequent new writes. Configuration builders do not
+collect owner evidence or convert schema-1 embedded files automatically.
+
+Use the [ADR 0006 migration runbook](adr/0006-tenant-scoped-result-idempotency.md#operational-runbook-isolated-rehearsal-and-future-store-conversion)
+for exact mapping, backup, replay and rollback rules. These entry points and
+fixtures are implemented; PG17/PG18/redb final-boundary execution is unverified.
+No live migration or owner mapping is authorized by this API description.
 
